diff --git a/docs/requirements.rst b/docs/requirements.rst
index fede671..94d3990 100644
--- a/docs/requirements.rst
+++ b/docs/requirements.rst
@@ -72,6 +72,23 @@ Usage
 Reference
 ---------
 
+Requirements support :func:`copy.replace` on Python 3.13 and later. On older
+Python versions, call :meth:`Requirement.__replace__` directly:
+
+.. doctest::
+
+    >>> req = Requirement('requests[security]>=2.0; python_version >= "3"')
+    >>> req.__replace__(name="flask")
+    <Requirement('flask[security]>=2.0; python_version >= "3"')>
+
+The keyword arguments ``name``, ``url``, ``extras``, ``specifier``, and ``marker``
+have the same types as the corresponding attributes. Omitted fields are kept.
+The new requirement is validated and normalized as when parsing a string;
+invalid fields or combinations raise :class:`InvalidRequirement`. Specifier
+prerelease overrides are preserved, with independent copies of the specifier
+set and its specifiers.
+
 .. automodule:: packaging.requirements
     :members:
     :exclude-members: __init__, __new__
+    :special-members: __replace__
